3f]\nv4.4.beta2.official [a013481b0]\n\n### System information\n\nw10 64\n\n### Issue description\n\nYou may need to increase the volume to hear this video. Observe the video: with the project set to 18 physics and process FPS, the sound is not played in sync, meaning there are changes in the frequency (not the waveform frequency) at which the sound is played.\n\nThen, I set the project to 12 FPS, and now the sound plays with a constant frequency, without variation. Or at least, no noticeable changes in the frequency at which the sound is played.\n\nIn other words, it seems the finished signal of the AudioStreamPlayer (or something related to it) is not emitted AT THE SAME TIME consistently (for example, when the project is initially set to 18 FPS in the video), but there’s variability that causes the sound not to be played at a constant pace every time.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ecc6dcec-75b3-4dec-89d2-501de57cd6b4\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee the video\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Test audio.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18689880/Test.audio.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_e